</pre></div><p><a href="program-to-print-all-pronic-numbers-between-1-to-100">6) Program to print all Pronic numbers between 1 to 100</a></p><p>A number is said to be pronic number if it is a product of two consecutive numbers.</p><p>For examples:</p><p>6 = 2 x 3<br>72 = 8 x 9</br></p><p><strong>Input:</strong></p><div class="codeblock"><div class="dp-highlighter"><div class="bar"><div class="tools"> </div></div><ol class="dp-xml" start="1"><li class="alt"><span><span>range(1, 101)  </span></span></li></ol></div><textarea class="xml" name="code" style="display:none">range(1, 101)
